# Generated packs. `tools/split.py` produces them from the source pack; they are
# generated, not source, so they are not committed - the build regenerates them.
#
# Deliberately NOT inside build/: `gradlew clean` deletes build/, and the packs are
# an input to this build (they are its sub-projects), not an output. Putting them
# there made `clean` delete the thing it was about to build.
packs/
build/
.gradle/

# `modules.json` IS committed, unlike the packs it describes. It is the baseline the
# upstream canary diffs against: a split that silently loses a module or moves ids
# into the wrong pack still passes verification, and the only way to notice is to
# compare against a layout a human looked at once. `MACRO_REFS.txt` is committed for
# the same reason - it is a short list of ids that cannot be resolved statically and
# that a reader should know about.

# Editor / OS noise
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
